course: dictionary
lesson: 2874
title: Donna: a name, a word, a title
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which meaning is right. «Donna» is a good example. When Maddie's mum's friend Donna visits from Newcastle, Donna is a person's first name, so it is a capital letter and a name for a woman.
explain: Donna is also an Italian word meaning «woman» or «lady». Ask yourself what fits: in a sentence about Italy, a donna is a woman, not a girl's name. An old title, like «Madam», shows respect for a lady.
explain: The phrase «prima donna» is different again. The words «prima» and «donna» come together and mean the main woman singer in an opera. Informally, it can also describe a person who is vain and expects special treatment, so context shows which meaning the writer wants.
fact: «Donna» is a woman's first name, and it has a capital letter.
fact: In Italian, «donna» means «woman» or «lady».
fact: «Prima donna» means the main woman singer in an opera, and informally, a vain person who expects special treatment.
fact: «Madonna» means «my lady», a title of Mary, the mother of Jesus.
fact: «Gadgie» is Geordie for a bloke, as in «that gadgie was mental», meaning that bloke was mad.
exercise: In «Donna visits from Newcastle», what kind of word is Donna? | A loud noise | *A name | A colour | A type of fish
exercise: The Italian word «donna» means what? | A type of bread | A small boat | A train station | *Woman or lady
exercise: Someone is called a «prima donna». What does the informal meaning suggest? | A cook for an opera | A very fast runner | A kind, quiet helper | *Vain and expecting special treatment
test: Which phrase means the main woman singer in an opera? | Donna visits | Madonna | Howay man | *Prima donna
test: In «Howay man, divvent be daft», what does the sentence tell you «divvent» means? | Perhaps | *Don't | Always | Very
exam: In «that gadgie was mental», what does gadgie mean? | A dog | *A bloke | A cloud | A fish
